## 7. Error Handling Strategy

### Error Categories and Response

| Error Category | Source | UI State | Retry Behavior |
|----------------|--------|----------|----------------|
| List query failure (initial) | Apollo `networkError` or `graphQLErrors` | `ErrorState` replaces card grid/table entirely — error banner with icon, message, "Retry" button | Retry button calls `refetch()` on Apollo query |
| Load More failure | Apollo `fetchMore` error | "Load More" button shows error state; existing cards remain; toast with retry option | User can click "Load More" again to retry |
| Create template failure | Apollo mutation error | Snackbar/toast with translated error message (`labels.errors.createFailed`) | User can retry from dialog (dialog stays open on error) |
| Duplicate template failure | Apollo mutation error | Snackbar with `labels.errors.duplicateFailed` | Card action menu remains available for retry |
| Delete template failure | Apollo mutation error | Snackbar with `labels.errors.deleteFailed` | DeleteConfirmDialog stays open on error; user can retry |
| Bulk action failure (partial) | `BatchResult.failures[]` | Results dialog showing success count + per-item failure list with error messages | User can retry failed items individually (future enhancement — current: show toast with failure count) |
| Bulk action failure (complete) | Apollo mutation error | Snackbar with translated error message | User can retry from bulk action bar |
| Category list failure (Plan 09 not ready) | Apollo query error or `skip` | Category filter dropdown shows disabled state with tooltip "Categories coming soon" | Automatic retry when Plan 09 becomes available (query refetches on mount) |
| Permission denied (mutation) | GraphQL error `FORBIDDEN` | Snackbar with `labels.errors.permissionDenied` | Action button becomes hidden (UI gate) |
| Network timeout | Apollo `networkError` | `ErrorState` with retry | Retry button refetches |

### Apollo Error Handling in Container

The container processes Apollo errors from `useQuery` and `useMutation`:

1. **Query errors**: `error.networkError` → network error state (ErrorState component); `error.graphQLErrors` → iterate, extract error codes, display translated messages via `labels.errors.*` keys
2. **Mutation errors**: `onError` callback → snackbar with translated error message from `labels.errors.*`; cache is NOT rolled back automatically (Apollo handles optimistic rollback if used)
3. **Batch mutation results**: `BatchResult.failures` array → snackbar showing "N items failed" with option for details dialog. If all succeed → success toast with count
4. **URL hydration errors**: If `cursor` in URL is invalid, the server returns an error — the container catches this, resets `cursor` to null, and re-fetches the first page

### Error State Components

| Component | When Used | Behavior |
|-----------|-----------|----------|
| `ErrorState` (full-page) | List query fails on initial load | Shows error title + description + retry button. Replaces the card grid/table entirely. Uses `labels.errors.loadFailed` and `labels.errors.retry` |
| `ErrorState` (load more) | `fetchMore` fails | "Load More" button shows error state inline; existing cards remain visible; retry by clicking button again |
| `ErrorToast` / Snackbar | Mutation fails | Auto-dismissing toast (4 seconds) with translated error message. Does not block UI. Uses `Snackbar` from MUI with `severity="error"` |
| `BatchResultToast` | Bulk action completes with partial failures | Toast showing "N succeeded, M failed" with action button to view details |

