## 10. Outcome & Knowledge Transfer Protocol

### 10.1 Deviation Log

Any pattern deviation from `siraj_analysis/05-frontend-patterns.md` discovered during implementation SHALL be documented inline as a comment in the relevant file AND logged to the session `todos` table with a `deviation` label.

### 10.2 Knowledge Artifacts for Plan 21

This plan produces the following knowledge that Plan 21 (Knowledge Propagation) will incorporate into permanent documentation:

| Artifact | Target Location |
|---|---|
| Template list card grid + table toggle pattern | `docs/certificates/frontend-list-patterns.md` (created in Plan 21) |
| URL-persisted filter state with Zustand mirror pattern | `docs/certificates/frontend-list-patterns.md` |
| Cursor pagination "Load More" with Apollo `fetchMore` | `docs/certificates/frontend-list-patterns.md` |
| Bulk action bar (sticky bottom) pattern with permission gating | `docs/certificates/frontend-list-patterns.md` |
| Arabic pluralization for count displays (6-form CLDR) | `docs/certificates/i18n-patterns.md` (created in Plan 21) |
| Sidebar navigation group registration pattern | `docs/certificates/navigation.md` (created in Plan 21) |
| Graceful degradation for cross-plan dependencies (category filter) | `docs/certificates/cross-plan-dependencies.md` (created in Plan 21) |
| i18n keys for template list page | `shared/locale/` type schema + en/ar implementations (done in this plan) |

### 10.3 Handoff to Plan 10 (Desktop Editor)

Plan 10 (Desktop Editor) consumes:
- Navigation route `/certificates/templates/{id}/editor` from this plan's card click action
- The template `id` passed as a URL parameter
- The Apollo cache entry from this plan's list query (Plan 10 can read cached template data from the list query if the editor query uses the same `id`-based cache normalization)
- The `createTemplate` mutation result (after creating a template, the container navigates to the editor with the new template's `id`)

### 10.4 Handoff to Plan 11 (Mobile Editor)

Plan 11 (Mobile Editor) consumes the same navigation route and cache entry as Plan 10, but renders the mobile-tier editor view.

### 10.5 Handoff to Plan 15 (Preview)

Plan 15 (Preview) is triggered from the card action menu "Preview" item. The container calls `router.push('/certificates/templates/{id}/preview')`. Plan 15 renders the preview UI (modal or page — decided by Plan 15). The template `id` is passed as a URL parameter.

### 10.6 Handoff to Plan 17 (Generate from Template)

Plan 17 (Generate from Template) is triggered from the card action menu "Generate from Template" item — visible only for published templates. The container calls `router.push('/certificates/generate/{id}')`. Plan 17 renders the generation wizard. The template `id` is passed as a URL parameter.

### 10.7 Handoff to Plan 09 (Categories)

Plan 09 (Categories) consumes:
- The sidebar navigation entry registered in this plan (Plan 08) under the "Certificates" group
- The route `/certificates/categories` — already listed in the sidebar config from this plan
- The `CategoryListQueryDocument` defined in this plan's GraphQL documents file — Plan 09 can reuse or extend this document for its own category tree queries

