## Reality Check Notes

> Audit performed against the live codebase at `/home/ahmed/Projects/siraj-cert/` (2026-08-02). Path/code-pattern corrections were applied across `requirements.md` / `design.md` / `tasks.md`; findings are summarised here.

### Verified Against Actual Codebase

| Check | Reference (actual codebase) | Plan Alignment |
|-------|------------------------------|----------------|
| Store location | `frontend/common/stores/` exists (~60 store files, e.g. `adminBillingStore.ts`, `dashboardStore.ts`, `entityStore.ts`, `studentListStore.ts`); `frontend/stores/` does **NOT** exist. Zustand conventions documented in `frontend/common/stores/AGENTS.md` (create-store helper, `StorageType` "persist"|"memory", selector hooks `useEntityStore(state => ...)`, NO `react-redux`, GraphQL types imported from `@/frontend/common/graphql/generated/gql/graphql-types` not `operations.ts`). | ✅ After correction. Originally referenced `frontend/stores/templateListStore.ts`; corrected to `frontend/common/stores/templateListStore.ts` (incl. `.types.ts`, `__mocks__/templateListStore.ts`). |
| Import alias | `@/frontend/common/stores/...` (matches the `@/frontend/common/...` alias used across the app). | ✅ Originally `@/frontend/stores/...`; corrected everywhere to `@/frontend/common/stores/...`. |
| sharedDocuments pattern | `frontend/common/graphql/sharedDocuments/<subdir>/<entity>.documents.ts` + `<subdir>/index.ts` barrel, re-exported by top-level `frontend/common/graphql/sharedDocuments/index.ts`. Conventions from `frontend/common/graphql/sharedDocuments/AGENTS.md`: `id` field mandatory in every selection; import Apollo hooks from `@apollo/client/react`; **`useLazyQuery` is banned**; operations are co-located. Existing example: `sharedDocuments/billing/invoice.documents.ts`. | ✅ Plan's `sharedDocuments/cert/template-list.documents.ts` + `sharedDocuments/cert/index.ts` barrel match the per-entity-file under a sub-directory barrel pattern. |
| Three-location view split (desktop / mobile) | `frontend/desktop/views/dashboard/<domain>/...` and `frontend/mobile/views/dashboard/<domain>/...` — each contains ONLY a `dashboard/` directory, which is then sub-divided per domain (admin, billing, classes, classes-sessions, parents, subjects, students, …). NO bare `frontend/{tier}/views/<domain>/` exists. | ✅ After correction. Originally referenced `frontend/desktop/views/certificates/...` and `frontend/mobile/views/certificates/...`; corrected to `frontend/desktop/views/dashboard/certificates/templates/...` and `frontend/mobile/views/dashboard/certificates/templates/...` (per-existing-domain convention). |
| App Router structure | `app/(dashboard)/<domain>/page.tsx` and `app/(dashboard)/<domain>/[entity]/...` (e.g. `app/(dashboard)/billing/invoices/page.tsx`, `app/(dashboard)/subjects/page.tsx`). No `app/(dashboard)/certificates/` route yet (to be added per the plan). | ✅ Plan's `app/(dashboard)/certificates/templates/page.tsx` matches the established `app/(dashboard)/<domain>/page.tsx` pattern. Routing wrapper + client island components pattern aligns with existing pages. |
| AGENTS conventions | `frontend/common/stores/AGENTS.md` (store rules), `frontend/common/views/AGENTS.md`, `frontend/views/AGENTS.md`, `frontend/common/graphql/AGENTS.md`. | ✅ References to `frontend/stores/AGENTS.md` corrected to `frontend/common/stores/AGENTS.md` in `design.md`, `tasks.md`, and `requirements.md`. |

### Corrections Made During Reality Check

1. **Store path** — `frontend/stores/templateListStore.ts` (and `.types.ts`, `__mocks__/templateListStore.ts`) → `frontend/common/stores/templateListStore.ts`. `frontend/stores/` does not exist; the actual store directory is `frontend/common/stores/`.
2. **Store imports** — `@/frontend/stores/...` → `@/frontend/common/stores/...` (consistent with the `@/frontend/common/...` alias).
3. **AGENTS reference** — `frontend/stores/AGENTS.md` → `frontend/common/stores/AGENTS.md` (multiple occurrences across design/tasks).
4. **Desktop view path** — `frontend/desktop/views/certificates/...` → `frontend/desktop/views/dashboard/certificates/templates/...` (the `views/` tree only contains a `dashboard/` directory; per-domain subdivisions sit inside `dashboard/`).
5. **Mobile view path** — `frontend/mobile/views/certificates/...` → `frontend/mobile/views/dashboard/certificates/templates/...` (same reason).

All replacements were verified with `grep -rn 'frontend/stores/' .ai/draft_plans/cert/plans/08-template-list-nav/` (zero matches remaining) and `grep -rn 'views/certificates/' ...` (zero matches remaining).

### Notes (no correction needed)

- The plan's per-tier component split (`TemplateList.desktop.tsx`, `TemplateList.mobile.tsx`) follows the established `frontend/{desktop,mobile}/views/dashboard/<domain>/components/<Entity>.<tier>.tsx` pattern.
- Zustand store shape (selector hooks, no `react-redux`, `StorageType` persist-vs-memory flag, types from generated GraphQL package not operations) matches `frontend/common/stores/AGENTS.md`.
- sharedDocuments is co-located with its domain; the `{ entity }.documents.ts` file name and the sub-directory barrel pattern are confirmed by other domains (e.g. `billing/invoice.documents.ts`, `students/student.documents.ts`).
- The plan's i18n reference to `shared/locale/{types,namespaces,en,ar}/dashboard/certificates/templates/list.ts` matches the verified per-feature locale convention (`<feature>.namespace.ts` + `<feature>.ts` under `dashboard/<domain>/`); see `shared/locale/namespaces/dashboard/subjects/main.namespace.ts` for a working example.

