## Round 4 Enhancement — Production Hardening

This section specifies production-grade UX concerns: accessibility, loading states, empty states, error handling, pagination, search, bulk actions, responsive behavior, performance budgets, and keyboard shortcuts. All MUI v9 conventions require `sx` prop usage (no style props). All imports use `@/*` path alias. Apollo hooks from `@apollo/client/react`, and i18n from `@/shared/locale/client`.

### 11.5 Accessibility & ARIA specification

All interactive elements must be keyboard navigable with a sensible tab order. Screen reader announcements fire on dynamic content updates.

**Tab order** (top-to-bottom, focus ring must be visible — never `outline: none` without replacement):

| # | Element | Role |
|---|---------|------|
| 1 | Page H1 `Typography` (heading only, not tab-stop) | `h1` |
| 2 | Global search `TextField` | `searchbox` |
| 3 | "New Template" `LoadingButton` | `button` |
| 4 | View mode toggle (`ToggleButtonGroup`) | `group` |
| 5 | Filter chips (each `Chip`) | `button` |
| 6 | "Apply Filters" / "Clear Filters" `Button`s | `button` |
| 7 | First template card or first row of `Table` | `article` / `row` |
| 8 | Sort selector (`Select`) | `combobox` |
| 9 | Page size selector (`Select`) | `combobox` |
| 10 | Load more `Button` (if infinite scroll) | `button` |

**ARIA labels & roles:**

```tsx
<TextField
  placeholder={t('search.placeholder')}
  aria-label={t('search.aria.label')}
  slotProps={{ htmlInput: { 'aria-label': t('search.aria.label') } }}
/>
<LoadingButton
  aria-label={t('create.button.aria.label')}
  startIcon={<AddOutlined />}
>
  {t('create.button.label')}
</LoadingButton>
<Chip
  label={t('filter.category.academic')}
  onDelete={handleRemove}
  aria-label={t('filter.chip.remove.aria', { name: t('filter.category.academic') })}
/>
```

**Screen reader live region** for list count and filter change announcements (place once near top of `TemplateListPage`):

```tsx
<Box role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" sx={{ position: 'absolute', width: 1, height: 1, margin: -1, padding: 0, overflow: 'hidden', clip: 'rect(0,0,0,0)', border: 0 }}>
  {t('aria.listCount', { count: visibleTemplates.length })}
</Box>
```

On filter/search change, the region text swaps so screen readers announce "N templates found". Use the `aria-live="polite"` setting so announcements don't interrupt the user.

**Focus trap for modals** — `CreateTemplateDialog` uses `@mui/utils` `unstable_TrapFocus` or the native `Dialog` focus trap (enabled by default in MUI v9). After dialog open, focus moves to the first tabbable field. On close, focus returns to the trigger button (track `previousActiveElement` via a ref).

**Modal focus trap spec:**

```tsx
const triggerRef = useRef<HTMLButtonElement>(null);
const [dialogOpen, setDialogOpen] = useState(false);
const handleOpen = () => { setDialogOpen(true); };
const handleClose = () => { setDialogOpen(false); triggerRef.current?.focus(); };
```

**Reduced motion support** — honor `prefers-reduced-motion` via `useMediaQuery('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)')`:

```tsx
const prefersReducedMotion = useMediaQuery('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
// Card hover, list reorder, skeleton shimmer animations disabled when true
<Card sx={{ transition: prefersReducedMotion ? 'none' : 'transform 150ms ease' }} />
<Skeleton animation={prefersReducedMotion ? false : 'wave'} />
```

**Additional ARIA requirements:**

| Element | ARIA attribute | Value |
|---------|---------------|-------|
| View mode toggle | `aria-label` | `t('viewMode.toggle.aria.label')` |
| Each toggle button | `aria-pressed` | `true \| false` (MUI sets automatically) |
| Filter bottom sheet `Drawer` | `aria-label` | `t('filter.sheet.aria.label')` |
| `Table` head | `scope="col"` on `TableCell` | Set per column header |
| Selection checkbox in row | `aria-label` | `t('row.select.aria', { name: template.name })` |
| Bulk action bar | `role="region"` | + `aria-label={t('bulkActionbar.aria')}` |
| Error banner | `role="alert"` | Set on the container `Alert` |
| Empty state illustration | `role="img"` + `aria-label` | `t('empty.illustration.aria')` |

**Keyboard navigation in `Table`:** `ArrowDown`/`ArrowUp` move between rows (call `rowRefs[idx].focus()`). `Enter` opens edit. `Space` toggles selection. `Shift+F` moves focus to filter bar.

### 11.6 Loading & Skeleton States

**Skeleton placeholder for card grid:**

```tsx
const SkCard = () => (
  <Card sx={{ display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', gap: 2 }}>
    <Skeleton variant="rectangular" width="100%" height={160} animation="wave" />
    <CardContent>
      <Skeleton variant="text" width="80%" height={28} animation="wave" />
      <Skeleton variant="text" width="50%" height={20} animation="wave" />
      <Skeleton variant="text" width="60%" height={20} animation="wave" />
    </CardContent>
  </Card>
);
```

Repeat `Array.from({ length: 8 })` for the full grid. The skeleton grid should match Card Grid `Grid` columns at each breakpoint to avoid layout shift during load.

**Skeleton placeholder for table view:**

```tsx
const SkRow = () => (
  <TableRow>
    <TableCell><Skeleton variant="text" width="60%" animation="wave" /></TableCell>
    {/* one cell per column */}
  </TableRow>
);
```

Add 10 skeleton rows under the existing table header.

**Progressive loading with intersection observer** — a `LoadMore` sentinel at the end of the list triggers the next page fetch when it scrolls into view:

```tsx
const sentinelRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
useIntersectionObserver(sentinelRef, () => { if (hasNextPage && !loading) loadMore(); });
return (
  <Box>
    {templates.map(...)}
    <Box ref={sentinelRef} sx={{ height: 20 }} aria-hidden />
    {loading && <CircularProgress sx={{ mx: 'auto', display: 'block' }} />}
  </Box>
);
```

**Stale-while-revalidate pattern (Apollo `useQuery` v4):**

```tsx
const { data, loading, error, fetchMore } = useQuery(CERT_TEMPLATES_QUERY, {
  variables: { input: { limit, offset } },
  fetchPolicy: 'cache-and-network',
  nextFetchPolicy: 'cache-first',
  notifyOnNetworkStatusChange: true,
});
```

On the first load, `loading` is true and skeletons show. On refresh, `data` already has cached values, `loading` is brief, and the stale list remains visible until new data arrives — no blank screen flash.

**Optimistic updates** — `deleteTemplate`, `duplicateTemplate`, and `favoriteTemplate` update the local state before the mutation returns, with rollback on error (DD-6). The store uses a `pendingOptimisticUpdates: Set<string>` field so other hooks can mark items as "pending" (e.g. dim text, show overlay).

**Loading shimmer spec:**

| State | UI | Duration target |
|-------|----|----------------|
| Initial list load | Skeleton grid (8 cards) | < 300ms shimmer cycle |
| Subsequent page | Append `CircularProgress` to list | — |
| Filter change | Keep current list, overlay low-opacity scrim | < 500ms shake off |
| Mutation in flight | `LoadingButton` spinner + dimmed row | — |
| Refetch | Keep stale list, no spinner | — |

### 11.7 Empty States

The `TemplateListPage` must show distinct empty states for five sub-cases. All states live in a `TemplateEmptyState` component with `variant` prop. All buttons use `LoadingButton` where a mutation is triggered.

**No templates yet (`variant="none"`):**

```tsx
<Box sx={{ display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', alignItems: 'center', gap: 3, py: 8, px: 2 }}>
  <Image alt={t('empty.none.illustration.aria')} src="/illustrations/empty-templates.svg" width={180} height={180} />
  <Typography variant="h5" sx={{ fontWeight: 600 }}>{t('empty.none.title')}</Typography>
  <Typography variant="body1" color="text.secondary" sx={{ maxWidth: 420, textAlign: 'center' }}>{t('empty.none.subtitle')}</Typography>
  <LoadingButton variant="contained" startIcon={<AddOutlined />} onClick={handleOpenCreateDialog}>{t('empty.none.cta')}</LoadingButton>
</Box>
```

**No search results (`variant="search"`):**

```tsx
<Typography variant="h6" sx={{ fontWeight: 600 }}>{t('empty.search.title', { query })}</Typography>
<Typography variant="body2" color="text.secondary">{t('empty.search.suggestions')}</Typography>
<Button onClick={handleClearSearch}>{t('empty.search.clearCta')}</Button>
// Suggestion chips:
<Stack direction="row" spacing={1} sx={{ flexWrap: 'wrap' }}>
  {suggestions.map(name => <Chip key={name} label={name} onClick={() => applySuggestion(name)} />)}
</Stack>
```

**No favorites (`variant="favorites"`):**

```tsx
<Typography variant="h6" sx={{ fontWeight: 600 }}>{t('empty.favorites.title')}</Typography>
<Typography variant="body2" color="text.secondary">{t('empty.favorites.subtitle')}</Typography>
<Button onClick={clearFavoriteFilter} variant="outlined">{t('empty.favorites.clearCta')}</Button>
```

**Filtered empty (`variant="filter"`):**

```tsx
<Typography variant="h6" sx={{ fontWeight: 600 }}>{t('empty.filter.title')}</Typography>
<Typography variant="body2" color="text.secondary">{t('empty.filter.subtitle')}</Typography>
<Button onClick={handleClearFilters} variant="outlined" startIcon={<CloseOutlined />}>{t('empty.filter.clearCta')}</Button>
```

**Error state with retry (`variant="error"`):**

```tsx
<Box role="alert">
  <Typography variant="h6" color="error.main" sx={{ fontWeight: 600 }}>{t('empty.error.title')}</Typography>
  <Typography variant="body2" color="text.secondary">{error}</Typography>
  <LoadingButton loading={retrying} onClick={handleRetry} variant="outlined" startIcon={<RefreshOutlined />}>{t('empty.error.retry')}</LoadingButton>
</Box>
```

### 11.8 Error Boundaries

A `TemplateListErrorBoundary` class component wraps `TemplateListPage` so a render exception doesn't blow up the entire dashboard. Categories: render error, query error, mutation error.

**Error boundary component spec:**

```tsx
class TemplateListErrorBoundary extends React.Component<{ fallback?: ReactNode; children: ReactNode }, { hasError: boolean; error: Error | null }> {
  state = { hasError: false, error: null };
  static getDerivedStateFromError(error: Error) { return { hasError: true, error }; }
  componentDidCatch(error: Error, info: React.ErrorInfo) {
    logger.error('TemplateListErrorBoundary', { error: error.message, info });
  }
  render() {
    if (this.state.hasError) return this.props.fallback ?? <DefaultErrorFallback error={this.state.error} onReset={() => this.setState({ hasError: false })} />;
    return this.props.children;
  }
}
```

The default fallback shows `Alert` with `severity="error"`, the error message (i18n-keyed but logged raw), and a "Try again" `LoadingButton` that resets state.

**Network error recovery** — add a 3-attempt exponential-backoff retry to `loadTemplates`:

```tsx
const attemptLoad = async (attempt = 0): Promise<void> => {
  try { await fetchTemplates(); }
  catch (err) {
    if (attempt >= 2) throw err;
    await sleep(2 ** attempt * 300);
    await attemptLoad(attempt + 1);
  }
};
```

After 3 failures, surface a persistent `Alert` with the retry button.

**Toast notification system** — use a `SnackbarProvider` from `@mui/joy`/MUI `Snackbar`:

```tsx
<SnackbarProvider maxSnack={3} anchorOrigin={{ vertical: 'bottom', horizontal: 'right' }}>
  <TemplateListPage />
</SnackbarProvider>
```

Trigger from store actions via a thin `enqueueToast(severity, messageKey, params)` API that lives in the store or a dedicated toast store.

**Offline indicator** — `navigator.onLine` polled via a `useOfflineStatus` hook; when false, show a persistent banner `<Alert severity="warning" variant="filled" sx={{ position: 'sticky', top: 0, zIndex: 'appBar' }}>{t('offline.banner')}</Alert>`. Persist pending mutations in a `retryQueue` indexed-db entry, replay on reconnect via a `useNetworkReconnect` effect.

**Retry queue spec:**

| Queue entry | Fields |
|-------------|--------|
| Mutation id | uuid |
| Operation name | `'deleteTemplate' \| 'duplicateTemplate' \| ...` |
| Variables | JSON-serializable |
| CreatedAt | ISO timestamp |
| Status | `'pending' \| 'in-flight' \| 'failed'` |

Replay on reconnect: enqueue all `'pending'` entries, run sequentially, log failures.

### 11.9 Pagination & Virtualization

**Infinite scroll with intersection observer** — default for card grid on mobile/tablet. Sentinel triggers `fetchMore({ variables: { input: { offset: templates.length, limit: PAGE_SIZE } }, updateQuery: (prev, { fetchMoreResult }) => prev.templates.concat(fetchMoreResult.templates) })`.

**Page size selector** — `Select` with options (`10, 20, 50, 100`), persisted in store as `pageSize`. Returns user to top of list on change.

**Total count display:** `Typography variant="caption"` near the list header:

```tsx
<Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary" sx={{ mr: 1 }}>{t('list.count', { total: totalCount, shown: visibleTemplates.length })}</Typography>
```

**Virtualized table for desktop** — when `pageSize >= 50` and row count exceeds 100, switch from raw `Table` to a `react-window` `FixedSizeList`:

```tsx
import { FixedSizeList } from 'react-window';
const Row = ({ index, style }) => (<div style={style}><TemplateTableRow template={templates[index]} /></div>);
return (
  <FixedSizeList height={600} itemCount={templates.length} itemSize={56} width="100%">
    {Row}
  </FixedSizeList>
);
```

Sticky header stays outside the virtualized list — render the `TableHead` separately. Cell measurement must match the non-virtualized row height to avoid clipping.

**Pagination for card grid** — when infinite scroll is disabled (accessibility setting `disableInfiniteScroll`), show a `TablePagination` at the bottom:

```tsx
<TablePagination
  component="div"
  count={totalCount}
  page={page}
  rowsPerPage={pageSize}
  onPageChange={(_, p) => setPage(p)}
  rowsPerPageOptions={[10, 20, 50, 100]}
  labelRowsPerPage={t('pagination.rowsPerPage')}
  labelDisplayedRows={({ from, to, count }) => t('pagination.range', { from, to, count })}
/>
```

### 11.10 Advanced Search & Filters

**Full-text search with debouncer** — the search `TextField` is debounced (300ms) using `useDebouncedCallback` from `use-debounce`:

```tsx
const debouncedSearch = useDebouncedCallback((q: string) => setDebouncedQuery(q), 300);
return <TextField onChange={(e) => { setQuery(e.target.value); debouncedSearch(e.target.value); }} />;
```

Search is passed to Apollo via `input.search` and matched server-side against name + description. Client-side fallback filter runs on already-fetched items for instant feedback before the network response arrives.

**Filter chips with remove** — active filters are rendered as removable `Chip`s above the list:

```tsx
const activeFilterChips = buildChips(filters);
activeFilterChips.map(chip => (
  <Chip key={chip.key} label={chip.label} onDelete={() => removeFilter(chip.key)} deleteIcon={<CloseOutlined />} />
));
```

**Saved filter presets** — `Menu` under a "Save filter" button:

```tsx
<Menu>
  <MenuItem onClick={handleOpenSaveDialog}>{t('filters.saveNew')}</MenuItem>
  {filterPresets.map(p => <MenuItem key={p.id} onClick={() => applyPreset(p.id)}>{p.name}</MenuItem>)}
</Menu>
```

Presets stored in a separate Zustand store (`templateFilterPresetStore`) keyed by user id; persisted in `localStorage`.

**Filter URL sync** — every filter change updates `searchParams` via `next/navigation` `useSearchParams`:

```tsx
const searchParams = useSearchParams();
const updateUrl = (patch: Record<string, string | null>) => {
  const next = new URLSearchParams(searchParams);
  Object.entries(patch).forEach(([k, v]) => v == null ? next.delete(k) : next.set(k, v));
  router.replace(`?${next.toString()}`, { scroll: false });
};
```

Dark-mode reads initial state from `searchParams` on mount.

**Date range picker** — use MUI `DateRangePicker` from `@mui/x-date-pickers-pro` for filtering by "modified in range":

```tsx
<DateRangePicker
  label={t('filters.dateRange')}
  value={dateRange}
  onChange={setDateRange}
  slotProps={{ textField: { sx: { width: 260 } } }}
/>
```

**Multi-select status filter** — `Select` with `multiple` on statuses (`Draft`, `Published`, `Archived`):

```tsx
<Select multiple value={selectedStatuses} onChange={e => setSelectedStatuses(e.target.value)} renderValue={(selected) => selected.join(', ')}><MenuItem value="draft">{t('status.draft')}</MenuItem> ...</Select>
```

### 11.11 Bulk Actions

**Select-all with indeterminate state** — the header row checkbox uses `indeterminate={selectedIds.length > 0 && selectedIds.length < totalCount}`.

```tsx
const allSelected = selectedIds.length === totalCount;
const indeterminate = selectedIds.length > 0 && !allSelected;
<Checkbox indeterminate={indeterminate} checked={allSelected} onChange={toggleSelectAll} />
```

**Bulk archive/delete/duplicate** — the bulk action bar appears when `selectedIds.length > 0`:

```tsx
{selectedIds.length > 0 && (
  <AppBar position="sticky" sx={{ bottom: 0, top: 'auto' }}>
    <Toolbar>
      <Typography>{t('bulkActionbar.count', { count: selectedIds.length })}</Typography>
      <LoadingButton onClick={handleBulkArchive} startIcon={<ArchiveOutlined />}>{t('bulk.archive')}</LoadingButton>
      <LoadingButton onClick={handleBulkDuplicate} startIcon={<FileCopyOutlined />}>{t('bulk.duplicate')}</LoadingButton>
      <LoadingButton color="error" onClick={handleBulkDelete} startIcon={<DeleteOutlined />}>{t('bulk.delete')}</LoadingButton>
    </Toolbar>
  </AppBar>
)}
```

**Confirmation dialogs with count** — bulk destructive actions show a confirmation dialog with the affected count, only accepting the action by typing "DELETE" in a `TextField`. Use `Dialog` with `aria-describedby` pointing at the count text.

**Undo toast with timeout** — archive actions emit a `Snackbar` with "Undo" action, auto-hiding after 5 seconds:

```tsx
enqueueToast({ severity: 'info', message: t('toast.archived.banner', { count }), action: <Button color="secondary" onClick={undoBulkArchive}>{t('toast.undo')}</Button>, autoHideDuration: 5000 });
```

After 5 seconds the archive is committed; before, `undoBulkArchive` iterates selected ids calling `unarchiveTemplate`.

**Bulk export** — export selected ids as a single CSV/ZIP package; the button triggers a mutation `bulkExportTemplatesMutationDocument`, and the server returns a signed download URL. Then a hidden `<a href={url} download>` programmatically clicks.

### 11.12 Responsive Breakpoints

Use MUI `sx` `display` object keys, `Grid` `size` (not `xs`/`md`/`lg` props — currently `size` mapping uses `size={{ xs: 12, md: 6, lg: 4 }}`). MUI v9 Grid uses new `size` API — confirm against project MUI version.

| Range | Layout | Grid cols | Bottom nav |
|-------|--------|-----------|------------|
| Mobile (< 768px) | Single-column card stack | 1 | Yes (bottom) |
| Tablet (768–1024px) | 2-column grid | 2 | No (sidebar) |
| Desktop (1024–1279px) | 3-column grid | 3 | No |
| Wide (> 1279px) | 4-column grid or table view | 4 or table | No |
| 4K | max 1400px wide centered container | 4 or table | No |

4K container wraps the page:

```tsx
<Box sx={{ maxWidth: 1400, mx: 'auto', px: { xs: 2, md: 4 } }}>
```

Mobile below-nav fixed height = `calc(100dvh - 56px)` to ensure the list scroll area sits under the bottom navigation bar.`Table` switches to card-list below the `sm` breakpoint: render `TemplateCard` components in a single-column `Stack` instead of `Table`.

### 11.13 Performance Budgets

| Metric | Budget | How ensured |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| LCP (Largest Contentful Paint) | < 2.5s on 4G mobile | Lazy-load illustration SVGs, inline critical CSS via Next.js |
| INP (Interaction to Next Paint) | < 200ms | Debounce search 300ms, virtualize > 100 rows, memoize row/cell with `React.memo` |
| CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift) | < 0.1 | Reserve skeleton slot dimensions, avoid post-load font swap |
| Bundle size (list chunk) | < 50 KB gzipped | Dynamic import `CreateTemplateDialog`, `LoadMore` sentinel, illustrations |
| API response (templates query) | p95 < 200ms | Backend uses cursor pagination, `limit: 20` default, indexes on `status`, `category`, `name` |
| List render per item | < 16ms | `React.memo` on `TemplateCard`/row, keying by template id, no inline object props |

Add a `useMemo` for derived props:

```tsx
const sortableTemplates = useMemo(() => applySort(templates, sortBy), [templates, sortBy]);
const visibleTemplates = useMemo(() => applyFilters(sortableTemplates, filters), [sortableTemplates, filters]);
```

Profile via React DevTools Profiler + Lighthouse; record baseline at start of Round 4 implementation.

### 11.14 Keyboard Shortcuts

Use a `useHotkeys` hook (from `react-hotkeys-hook`) or a custom reducer in `TemplateListPage`. Shortcuts are scoped to the page via a `ref` container with `tabIndex={-1}` to capture keydown. All shortcuts show in a "Keyboard shortcuts" dialog triggered by `?`.

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `/` | Focus search input |
| `n` | Open "New Template" dialog |
| `r` | Refresh list |
| `Esc` | Clear all filters (or close dialog if open) |
| `Cmd+A` (Mac) / `Ctrl+A` (others) | Select all visible templates |
| `ArrowDown` / `ArrowUp` | Move focus between rows in table view |
| `Enter` | Open edit for focused row |
| `Space` | Toggle row selection (focused row) |
| `?` | Open keyboard shortcuts dialog |
| `g` then `c` | Go to cards view (chord) |
| `g` then `t` | Go to table view (chord) |

**Hook spec:**

```tsx
import { useHotkeys } from 'react-hotkeys-hook';
useHotkeys('/', (e) => { e.preventDefault(); searchRef.current?.focus(); });
useHotkeys('n', () => openCreateDialog());
useHotkeys('esc', () => clearFilters());
useHotkeys('mod+a', (e) => { e.preventDefault(); selectAll(); });
useHotkeys('?', () => setShortcutsDialogOpen(true));
```

Shortcuts are disabled when a modal is open (focus trap consumes them) and when the active element is a `TextField`, `Textarea`, or `Select`. Display shortcut hints next to their controls as `Tooltip` with the key sequence.

### 11.15 Round 4 i18n Key Catalog Addendum

New shared locale namespaces (`shared/locale/en/certTemplates.ts`, `shared/locale/ar/certTemplates.ts`):

| Namespace key | Usage |
|---------------|-------|
| `aria.listCount` | Live region count announcement |
| `search.aria.label` | Search input label |
| `create.button.aria.label` | New template button label |
| `filter.chip.remove.aria` | Filter chip remove label |
| `viewMode.toggle.aria.label` | View mode toggle group label |
| `filter.sheet.aria.label` | Mobile filter sheet title |
| `row.select.aria` | Row selection checkbox label |
| `bulkActionbar.aria` | Bulk action bar region label |
| `empty.none.*` | No templates state strings |
| `empty.search.*` | No search results strings |
| `empty.favorites.*` | No favorites strings |
| `empty.filter.*` | Filtered empty strings |
| `empty.error.*` | Error retry strings |
| `pagination.rowsPerPage` | Rows per page label |
| `pagination.range` | Range display |
| `filters.saveNew` | Save filter preset |
| `list.count` | Count display |
| `bulk.*` | Bulk action labels |
| `toast.archived.banner` | Archive toast |
| `toast.undo` | Undo label |
| `offline.banner` | Offline banner |
| `shortcuts.*` | Shortcut dialog labels |

Each key must exist in both `en` and `ar` files. Pluralizable keys use the `(count: number) => string` signature as defined in `shared/AGENTS.md`.

### 11.16 Round 4 Store Interface Addendum

Updates to `TemplateListState` (in `frontend/stores/cert/templateListStore.ts`):

```typescript
interface TemplateListState {
  // Round 4 additions
  totalPages: number;
  currentPage: number;
  pageSize: number;
  hasNextPage: boolean;
  totalCount: number;
  debouncedQuery: string;
  selectedStatuses: string[];
  dateRange: { start: string | null; end: string | null };
  filterPresets: TemplateFilterPreset[];
  activePresetId: string | null;
  pendingOptimisticUpdates: string[];
  enqueueToast: (input: ToastInput) => void;
  undoBulkArchive: () => Promise<void>;
  bulkArchive: (ids: string[]) => Promise<void>;
  bulkDelete: (ids: string[]) => Promise<void>;
  bulkDuplicate: (ids: string[]) => Promise<void>;
  bulkExport: (ids: string[]) => Promise<string>;
  toggleSelectAll: () => void;
  setPageSize: (size: number) => void;
  setCurrentPage: (page: number) => void;
  setSelectedStatuses: (statuses: string[]) => void;
  setDateRange: (range: { start: string | null; end: string | null }) => void;
  saveFilterPreset: (name: string) => Promise<void>;
  applyFilterPreset: (id: string) => void;
  removeFilterPreset: (id: string) => Promise<void>;
  clearFilters: () => void;
  loadMore: () => Promise<void>;
  retryFailedMutations: () => Promise<void>;
}
```

### 11.17 Round 4 Apollo Document Addendum

New documents in `frontend/common/graphql/sharedDocuments/certTemplate.documents.ts`:

```typescript
// Cursor-based paginated query
export const CERT_TEMPLATES_PAGINATED_QUERY = gql`
  query CertTemplatesPaginated($input: CertTemplateListInput!) {
    certTemplates(input: $input) {
      items { id name description status category updatedAt createdAt }
      totalCount hasNextPage cursor
    }
  }
`;

// Bulk operations
export const BULK_ARCHIVE_CERT_TEMPLATES_MUTATION = gql`
  mutation BulkArchiveCertTemplates($input: BulkArchiveInput!) { bulkArchiveCertTemplates(input: $input) { id status } }
`;
export const BULK_DELETE_CERT_TEMPLATES_MUTATION = gql`
  mutation BulkDeleteCertTemplates($input: BulkDeleteInput!) { bulkDeleteCertTemplates(input: $input) { id } }
`;
export const BULK_DUPLICATE_CERT_TEMPLATES_MUTATION = gql`
  mutation BulkDuplicateCertTemplates($input: BulkDuplicateInput!) { bulkDuplicateCertTemplates(input: $input) { id name status } }
`;
export const BULK_EXPORT_CERT_TEMPLATES_MUTATION = gql`
  mutation BulkExportCertTemplates($input: BulkExportInput!) { bulkExportCertTemplates(input: $input) { downloadUrl expiresAt } }
`;
```

All mutations must include `id` for Apollo cache normalization. `BulkExport` returns a `downloadUrl` (signed) and `expiresAt`. Schema additions go in `backend/graphql/pothos/cert/template.ts` and services in `backend/services/cert/template.service.ts`.
